---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Experiment 7.1: Acceleration Due to Gravity">
    <main class="container mx-auto px-4 py-8">
        <div class="experiment-header">
            <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-center text-blue-700 mb-2">EXPERIMENT 7.1</h1>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-center text-blue-700 mb-8">ACCELERATION DUE TO GRAVITY</h2>
        </div>

        <!-- Email Collection Section -->
        <section class="mb-8">
            <div class="bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg mb-4">
                <h4 class="font-bold mb-2">Student Information:</h4>
                <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
                    <div>
                        <label for="studentName" class="block text-gray-700 font-bold mb-2">Name:</label>
                        <input type="text" id="studentName" class="w-full px-3 py-2 border rounded-lg" placeholder="Your Name">
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <label for="studentEmail" class="block text-gray-700 font-bold mb-2">Email:</label>
                        <input type="email" id="studentEmail" class="w-full px-3 py-2 border rounded-lg" placeholder="your.email@example.com">
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="mt-4">
                    <label for="teacherEmail" class="block text-gray-700 font-bold mb-2">Teacher's Email:</label>
                    <input type="email" id="teacherEmail" class="w-full px-3 py-2 border rounded-lg" value="chuck@c00lnerd.com" placeholder="teacher.email@example.com">
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Purpose Section -->
        <section class="mb-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-blue-700">PURPOSE:</h3>
            <p class="mb-4">To observe how acceleration due to gravity is independent of the object falling.</p>
        </section>

        <!-- Materials Section -->
        <section class="mb-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-blue-700">MATERIALS:</h3>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-8 mb-4">
                <li>A large heavy book (at least 21 cm by 27 cm)</li>
                <li>A small piece of paper (about 3 cm by 3 cm)</li>
                <li>Eye protection such as goggles or safety glasses</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- Safety Section -->
        <section class="mb-8">
            <div class="bg-yellow-50 border-l-4 border-yellow-400 p-4">
                <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-yellow-700">SAFETY:</h3>
                <ul class="list-disc pl-8 mb-0">
                    <li>Always wear eye protection when dropping objects.</li>
                    <li>Make sure the area below is clear of obstacles and people.</li>
                    <li>Be careful when handling heavy books to avoid injury.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Background Section -->
        <section class="mb-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-blue-700">BACKGROUND:</h3>
            <p class="mb-4">One of the properties of free fall is that all objects experience the same acceleration regardless of their weight or physical makeup. That tends to go against your everyday experience. This experiment shows you that it is, indeed, true.</p>
            <p class="mb-4">In the absence of air resistance, all objects fall at the same rate under the influence of gravity. This is because the acceleration due to gravity (approximately 9.8 m/s²) acts equally on all objects regardless of their mass. The force of gravity is proportional to an object's mass, but the acceleration produced is independent of mass because the greater force on a more massive object is offset by its greater inertia.</p>
            <p class="mb-4">However, in the real world, air resistance can significantly affect the motion of falling objects, especially those with large surface areas relative to their mass. This experiment will demonstrate both scenarios: objects falling with and without the influence of air resistance.</p>
        </section>

        <!-- Question Section -->
        <section class="mb-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-blue-700">QUESTION:</h3>
            <p class="mb-4">What happens when you drop two different objects at the same time? Do they hit the ground simultaneously?</p>
        </section>

        <!-- Hypothesis Section -->
        <section class="mb-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-blue-700">HYPOTHESIS:</h3>
            <p class="mb-4">Write what you predict will happen to the paper and the book when dropped from the same height at the same time. Will they hit the ground together, or will one hit before the other?</p>
            <div class="mb-4">
                <textarea id="hypothesis" class="w-full p-2 border rounded-lg" rows="4" placeholder="Write your hypothesis here..."></textarea>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Procedure Section -->
        <section class="mb-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-blue-700">PROCEDURE:</h3>
            <ol class="list-decimal pl-8 mb-4 space-y-4">
                <li>
                    <p>Hold the book in one hand and the paper in the other. Hold both of them out at arm's length, and make sure that they are at exactly the same height. Make sure that there are no obstructions beneath the two objects so that they can fall to the floor without running into something.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>Now, release them both at precisely the same instant. Note what happens. Specifically, note which object (the book or the paper) hits the ground first. If they hit simultaneously, note that.</p>
                    <div class="mt-2">
                        <label class="block text-gray-700 font-bold mb-2">Trial 1 Observation:</label>
                        <textarea id="trial1" class="w-full p-2 border rounded-lg" rows="2" placeholder="Record what you observed..."></textarea>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>Next, repeat the experiment in a slightly different way. This time place the piece of paper on top of the book and hold the book out at arm's length with both hands. Now release the book and paper. Note what happens this time.</p>
                    <div class="mt-2">
                        <label class="block text-gray-700 font-bold mb-2">Trial 2 Observation:</label>
                        <textarea id="trial2" class="w-full p-2 border rounded-lg" rows="2" placeholder="Record what you observed..."></textarea>
                    </div>
                </li>
            </ol>
        </section>

        <!-- Video Demonstration Section -->
        <section class="mb-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-blue-700">VIDEO DEMONSTRATION:</h3>
            <p class="mb-4">Watch this demonstration of the gravity experiment to see the concepts in action:</p>
            
            <div class="relative w-full max-w-2xl mx-auto">
                <div class="aspect-w-9 aspect-h-16 bg-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
                    <iframe 
                        src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/X5uKz67suXs" 
                        title="Acceleration Due to Gravity Experiment Demonstration"
                        frameborder="0" 
                        allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" 
                        allowfullscreen
                        class="w-full h-full">
                    </iframe>
                </div>
            </div>
            
            <div class="mt-4 p-4 bg-blue-50 rounded-lg">
                <h4 class="font-bold text-blue-700 mb-2">What to Look For:</h4>
                <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1 text-sm">
                    <li>Notice how objects fall when dropped together vs. separately</li>
                    <li>Observe the effect of air resistance on different objects</li>
                    <li>Pay attention to the timing of when objects hit the ground</li>
                    <li>Consider how this demonstrates the principles of gravity</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            
            <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-gray-600">
                <strong>Alternative Link:</strong> If the video doesn't load, you can watch it directly at: 
                <a href="https://www.youtube.com/shorts/X5uKz67suXs" target="_blank" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">
                    https://www.youtube.com/shorts/X5uKz67suXs
                </a>
            </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Analysis Questions Section -->
        <section class="mb-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-blue-700">ANALYSIS QUESTIONS:</h3>
            <div class="space-y-4">
                <div>
                    <p class="font-bold">1. In the first trial, which object hit the ground first? Why do you think this happened?</p>
                    <textarea id="question1" class="w-full p-2 border rounded-lg" rows="2" placeholder="Your answer..."></textarea>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <p class="font-bold">2. In the second trial, did the paper and book hit the ground at the same time? Explain why.</p>
                    <textarea id="question2" class="w-full p-2 border rounded-lg" rows="2" placeholder="Your answer..."></textarea>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <p class="font-bold">3. What force caused the difference in results between the two trials?</p>
                    <textarea id="question3" class="w-full p-2 border rounded-lg" rows="2" placeholder="Your answer..."></textarea>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <p class="font-bold">4. If you were to perform this experiment on the Moon (which has no atmosphere), how would the results differ from what you observed on Earth?</p>
                    <textarea id="question4" class="w-full p-2 border rounded-lg" rows="2" placeholder="Your answer..."></textarea>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <p class="font-bold">5. How does this experiment demonstrate Newton's Second Law of Motion?</p>
                    <textarea id="question5" class="w-full p-2 border rounded-lg" rows="2" placeholder="Your answer..."></textarea>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>



        <!-- Conclusion Section -->
        <section class="mb-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-blue-700">CONCLUSION:</h3>
            <p class="mb-4">Write a paragraph about what happened in the two trials you performed. Make connections to the text (specifically the paragraphs that follow).</p>
            <div class="mb-4">
                <textarea id="conclusion" class="w-full p-2 border rounded-lg" rows="6" placeholder="Write your conclusion here..."></textarea>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Extension Section -->
        <section class="mb-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-blue-700">EXTENSION:</h3>
            <p class="mb-4">Try this experiment with different objects of varying weights and shapes. How does air resistance affect the falling rate of different objects? Can you design an object that falls more slowly than a flat piece of paper?</p>
            <div class="mb-4">
                <textarea id="extension" class="w-full p-2 border rounded-lg" rows="4" placeholder="Record your extension activities here..."></textarea>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Submit Section -->
        <section class="mb-8">
            <div class="bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg">
                <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-blue-700 mb-4">SUBMIT YOUR RESULTS:</h3>
                <p class="mb-4">Click the button below to submit your experiment results to your teacher.</p>
                <button id="submitBtn" class="bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-700 text-white font-bold py-2 px-4 rounded">
                    Submit Results
                </button>
                <p id="submissionMessage" class="mt-2 hidden"></p>
            </div>
        </section>
    </main>
</Layout>

<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@emailjs/browser@3/dist/email.min.js"></script>
<script is:inline>
    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function() {
        // Initialize EmailJS (same key used in other experiments)
        emailjs.init('ct_s19oZHppLy9BlW');
        // Store student information in local storage
        const studentNameInput = document.getElementById('studentName');
        const studentEmailInput = document.getElementById('studentEmail');
        const teacherEmailInput = document.getElementById('teacherEmail');

        // Load stored values if they exist
        if (localStorage.getItem('studentName')) {
            studentNameInput.value = localStorage.getItem('studentName');
        }
        if (localStorage.getItem('studentEmail')) {
            studentEmailInput.value = localStorage.getItem('studentEmail');
        }
        if (localStorage.getItem('teacherEmail')) {
            teacherEmailInput.value = localStorage.getItem('teacherEmail');
        }

        // Save values when they change
        studentNameInput.addEventListener('change', function() {
            localStorage.setItem('studentName', this.value);
        });
        studentEmailInput.addEventListener('change', function() {
            localStorage.setItem('studentEmail', this.value);
        });
        teacherEmailInput.addEventListener('change', function() {
            localStorage.setItem('teacherEmail', this.value);
        });

        // Video tracking (YouTube embed doesn't need tracking)
        let videoWatched = true; // Assume video is available for viewing

        // Handle form submission
        const submitBtn = document.getElementById('submitBtn');
        const submissionMessage = document.getElementById('submissionMessage');

        submitBtn.addEventListener('click', function() {
            // Validate required fields
            const studentName = studentNameInput.value.trim();
            const studentEmail = studentEmailInput.value.trim();
            const teacherEmail = teacherEmailInput.value.trim();
            const hypothesis = document.getElementById('hypothesis').value.trim();
            const trial1 = document.getElementById('trial1').value.trim();
            const trial2 = document.getElementById('trial2').value.trim();
            const conclusion = document.getElementById('conclusion').value.trim();

            if (!studentName || !studentEmail || !teacherEmail) {
                showMessage('Please fill in all required student and teacher information.', 'error');
                return;
            }

            if (!hypothesis || !trial1 || !trial2 || !conclusion) {
                showMessage('Please complete your hypothesis, observations, and conclusion before submitting.', 'error');
                return;
            }

            // Collect answers to analysis questions
            const question1 = document.getElementById('question1').value.trim();
            const question2 = document.getElementById('question2').value.trim();
            const question3 = document.getElementById('question3').value.trim();
            const question4 = document.getElementById('question4').value.trim();
            const question5 = document.getElementById('question5').value.trim();
            const extension = document.getElementById('extension').value.trim();

            // Prepare comprehensive experiment data (matching working experiment3_2 structure)
            const questionsData = 
                '1. What happened when you dropped the book and paper together?\n' +
                (question1 || 'Not answered') + '\n\n' +
                '2. What happened when you dropped the book and paper separately?\n' +
                (question2 || 'Not answered') + '\n\n' +
                '3. Why did the paper fall more slowly when dropped by itself?\n' +
                (question3 || 'Not answered') + '\n\n' +
                '4. What does this experiment tell us about gravity and air resistance?\n' +
                (question4 || 'Not answered') + '\n\n' +
                '5. How might this experiment be different on the Moon?\n' +
                (question5 || 'Not answered');

            const experimentData = 
                'EXPERIMENT 7.1: ACCELERATION DUE TO GRAVITY - DETAILED RESULTS\n\n' +
                'Student: ' + studentName + '\n' +
                'Email: ' + studentEmail + '\n\n' +
                'HYPOTHESIS:\n' + hypothesis + '\n\n' +
                'TRIAL OBSERVATIONS:\n' +
                'Trial 1 (Book and Paper Together): ' + trial1 + '\n' +
                'Trial 2 (Book and Paper Separately): ' + trial2 + '\n\n' +
                'ANALYSIS QUESTIONS:\n' + questionsData + '\n\n' +
                'CONCLUSION:\n' + conclusion + '\n\n' +
                'EXTENSION ACTIVITIES:\n' + (extension || 'None provided') + '\n\n' +
                'Video Demonstration Watched: ' + (videoWatched ? 'Yes' : 'No') + '\n' +
                'Experiment completed: ' + new Date().toLocaleString();

            // Disable button and show loading state
            submitBtn.disabled = true;
            submitBtn.textContent = 'Submitting...';

            // Send email using EmailJS with exact parameter structure from working experiment3_2
            emailjs.send('service_ot1jg6s', 'template_y556rhr', {
                student_name: studentName,
                student_email: studentEmail,
                experiment_title: 'Experiment 7.1: Acceleration Due to Gravity',
                hypothesis: hypothesis || 'No hypothesis provided',
                missing_elements: questionsData,
                conclusion: experimentData,
                subject: `Experiment 7.1 - ${studentName}`
            })
                .then(function(response) {
                    console.log('SUCCESS!', response.status, response.text);
                    showMessage('Your experiment results have been submitted successfully!', 'success');
                    submitBtn.textContent = 'Submitted';
                })
                .catch(function(error) {
                    console.log('FAILED...', error);
                    showMessage('Failed to submit results. Please try again later.', 'error');
                    submitBtn.disabled = false;
                    submitBtn.textContent = 'Submit Results';
                });
        });

        function showMessage(message, type) {
            submissionMessage.textContent = message;
            submissionMessage.classList.remove('hidden', 'text-green-600', 'text-red-600');
            submissionMessage.classList.add(type === 'success' ? 'text-green-600' : 'text-red-600');
        }
    });
</script>
